.* QTOCHTE: CFGTCP option 10, the host table, one row per host name
.* (the address on an entry's first). WRKHTE has every option, WRKHTED
.* only 5=Display. DSPHTE is option 5.
:PNLGRP.
:COPYR.(C) COPYRIGHT QUARTZ SYSTEMS 2026.
:CLASS NAME=OPTCL BASETYPE=ACTION.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=ADRCL BASETYPE='CHAR 32'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=KEYCL BASETYPE='CHAR 45'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=HOSTCL BASETYPE='CHAR 255'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=TEXTCL BASETYPE='CHAR 64'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=VALCL BASETYPE='CHAR 45'.
:ECLASS.
:VAR NAME=OPT CLASS=OPTCL.
:VAR NAME=HTEADR CLASS=ADRCL.
:VAR NAME=HTEKEY CLASS=KEYCL.
:VAR NAME=HTENAME CLASS=HOSTCL.
:VAR NAME=DADR CLASS=VALCL.
:VAR NAME=DTEXT CLASS=TEXTCL.
:VAR NAME=DNAME CLASS=HOSTCL.
:LISTDEF NAME=HOSTS VARS='OPT HTEADR HTENAME HTEKEY'.
:LISTDEF NAME=NAMES VARS='DNAME'.
:KEYL NAME=WRKKEYS HELP='KEYS/WRKKEYS'.
:KEYI KEY=ENTER ACTION=ENTER.
:KEYI KEY=HELP ACTION=HELP.
:KEYI KEY=F1 ACTION=HELP.
:KEYI KEY=F3 ACTION=EXIT.F3=Exit
:KEYI KEY=F5 ACTION='RETURN 5'.F5=Refresh
:KEYI KEY=F6 ACTION='RETURN 6'.F6=Print list
:KEYI KEY=F12 ACTION=CANCEL.F12=Cancel
:KEYI KEY=F13 ACTION='RETURN 13'.F13=Sort by add sequence
:KEYI KEY=F17 ACTION='RETURN 17'.F17=Position to
:KEYI KEY=F22 ACTION='RETURN 22'.F22=Display entire field
:KEYI KEY=PAGEUP ACTION=PAGEUP.
:KEYI KEY=PAGEDOWN ACTION=PAGEDOWN.
:EKEYL.
:KEYL NAME=DSPKEYS HELP='KEYS/DSPKEYS'.
:KEYI KEY=ENTER ACTION=ENTER.
:KEYI KEY=HELP ACTION=HELP.
:KEYI KEY=F1 ACTION=HELP.
:KEYI KEY=F3 ACTION=EXIT.F3=Exit
:KEYI KEY=F12 ACTION=CANCEL.F12=Cancel
:KEYI KEY=F22 ACTION='RETURN 22'.F22=Display entire field
:KEYI KEY=PAGEUP ACTION=PAGEUP.
:KEYI KEY=PAGEDOWN ACTION=PAGEDOWN.
:EKEYL.
:PANEL NAME=WRKHTE HELP=HLPHTE KEYL=WRKKEYS ENTER='RETURN 0' TOPSEP=SYSNAM BOTSEP=NONE.Work with TCP/IP Host Table Entries
:TOPINST.Type options, press Enter.
:LIST DEPTH='*' LISTDEF=HOSTS SCROLL=YES ACTLEN=1 EXTACT=YES.(No host table entries)
:LISTACT OPTION=1 ACTFOR=EXTACT ENTER='CMD ?ADDTCPHTE INTNETADR(''&HTEADR.'')' HELP='WRKHTE/OPTIONS'.1=Add
:LISTACT OPTION=2 ACTFOR=LISTE ENTER='CMD ?CHGTCPHTE INTNETADR(''&HTEKEY.'')' HELP='WRKHTE/OPTIONS'.2=Change
:LISTACT OPTION=4 ACTFOR=LISTE ENTER='CMD RMVTCPHTE INTNETADR(''&HTEKEY.'')' HELP='WRKHTE/OPTIONS'.4=Remove
:LISTACT OPTION=5 ACTFOR=LISTE ENTER='RETURN 105' HELP='WRKHTE/OPTIONS'.5=Display
:LISTACT OPTION=7 ACTFOR=LISTE ENTER='CMD ?RNMTCPHTE INTNETADR(''&HTEKEY.'')' HELP='WRKHTE/OPTIONS'.7=Rename
:LISTCOL VAR=OPT USAGE=INPUT HELP='WRKHTE/OPT'.Opt
:LISTCOL VAR=HTEADR USAGE=OUTPUT EXTACT=YES HELP='FLD/HTEADR'.Internet                                  Address
:LISTCOL VAR=HTENAME USAGE=OUTPUT MAXWIDTH=38 HELP='FLD/HTENAME'.Host                                       Name
:LISTCOL VAR=HTEKEY USAGE=OUTPUT DISPLAY=NO.Key
:ELIST.
:EPANEL.
:PANEL NAME=WRKHTED HELP=HLPHTE KEYL=WRKKEYS ENTER='RETURN 0' TOPSEP=SYSNAM BOTSEP=NONE.Work with TCP/IP Host Table Entries
:TOPINST.Type options, press Enter.
:LIST DEPTH='*' LISTDEF=HOSTS SCROLL=YES ACTLEN=1 EXTACT=YES.(No host table entries)
:LISTACT OPTION=5 ACTFOR=LISTE ENTER='RETURN 105' HELP='WRKHTED/OPTIONS'.5=Display
:LISTCOL VAR=OPT USAGE=INPUT HELP='WRKHTED/OPT'.Opt
:LISTCOL VAR=HTEADR USAGE=OUTPUT EXTACT=YES HELP='FLD/HTEADR'.Internet                                  Address
:LISTCOL VAR=HTENAME USAGE=OUTPUT MAXWIDTH=38 HELP='FLD/HTENAME'.Host                                       Name
:LISTCOL VAR=HTEKEY USAGE=OUTPUT DISPLAY=NO.Key
:ELIST.
:EPANEL.
:PANEL NAME=DSPHTE HELP=HLPDSP KEYL=DSPKEYS ENTER='RETURN 0' TOPSEP=SYSNAM.Display TCP/IP Host Table Entry
:DATA DEPTH=5.
:DATACOL WIDTH=40.
:DATACOL WIDTH=78.
:DATAI VAR=DADR USAGE=OUTPUT HELP='FLD/DADR'.Internet address
:DATAC.
:DATAI VAR=DTEXT USAGE=OUTPUT HELP='FLD/DTEXT'.Text description
:EDATA.
:LIST DEPTH='*' LISTDEF=NAMES SCROLL=YES.
:LISTCOL VAR=DNAME USAGE=OUTPUT MAXWIDTH=77 HELP='FLD/DNAME'.Host                                                                                 Name
:ELIST.
:BOTINST.Press Enter to continue.
:EPANEL.
:HELP NAME=HLPHTE.Work with TCP/IP Host Table Entries - Help
:P.The host table: each address with its names, in address order (F13
shows them in the order they were added). Type an option next to an
address to change, remove, display or rename its entry; option 1 adds
one.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=HLPDSP.Display TCP/IP Host Table Entry - Help
:P.One address's names and text.
:EHELP.
.* Item, key and option help.
:HELP NAME='KEYS/WRKKEYS'.Function keys
:PARML.
:PT.F3=Exit
:PD.Ends the display and returns to where it was started from.
:PT.F5=Refresh
:PD.Shows the display again with the current information.
:PT.F6=Print list
:PD.Print list.
:PT.F12=Cancel
:PD.Returns to the previous display without acting on what was typed.
:PT.F13=Sort by add sequence
:PD.Sort by add sequence.
:PT.F17=Position to
:PD.Positions the list at the name typed on the command line.
:PT.F22=Display entire field
:PD.Display entire field.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKHTE/OPT'.Option
:P.Type the number of an option next to an entry and press Enter. The
options the list allows are shown above it; F1 on one of them explains
it.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/HTEADR'.Internet                                  Address
:P.The internet Address of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/HTENAME'.Host                                       Name
:P.The host Name of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKHTE/OPTIONS'.Options
:P.Type an option number next to one or more entries and press Enter.
The option runs for each entry it is typed next to, in order.
:PARML.
:PT.1=Add
:PD.Type 1 next to an entry and press Enter to add it. The Add TCP/IP
Host Table Entry (ADDTCPHTE) command is prompted for the entry.
:PT.2=Change
:PD.Type 2 next to an entry and press Enter to change it. The Change
TCP/IP Host Table Entry (CHGTCPHTE) command is prompted for the entry.
:PT.4=Remove
:PD.Type 4 next to an entry and press Enter to remove it. The Remove
TCP/IP Host Table Entry (RMVTCPHTE) command runs for the entry.
:PT.5=Display
:PD.Type 5 next to an entry and press Enter to display it.
:PT.7=Rename
:PD.Type 7 next to an entry and press Enter to rename it. The Rename
TCP/IP Host Table Entry (RNMTCPHTE) command is prompted for the entry.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKHTED/OPT'.Option
:P.Type the number of an option next to an entry and press Enter. The
options the list allows are shown above it; F1 on one of them explains
it.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKHTED/OPTIONS'.Options
:P.Type an option number next to one or more entries and press Enter.
The option runs for each entry it is typed next to, in order.
:PARML.
:PT.5=Display
:PD.Type 5 next to an entry and press Enter to display it.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='KEYS/DSPKEYS'.Function keys
:PARML.
:PT.F3=Exit
:PD.Ends the display and returns to where it was started from.
:PT.F12=Cancel
:PD.Returns to the previous display without acting on what was typed.
:PT.F22=Display entire field
:PD.Display entire field.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/DADR'.Internet address
:P.An internet address in dotted decimal form (IPv4) or in colon form
(IPv6).
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/DTEXT'.Text description
:P.The text description shown for what the display is about.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/DNAME'.Host                                                                                 Name
:P.The host Name of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:EPNLGRP.
